# Invention disclosure (the inventor's own words)

This is the ONLY authority for what the invention includes. Everything you claim must be supported here or in later messages from the user.

Handheld vacuum lifter with grip-loss alarm

A cordless handheld vacuum lifter is disclosed. The lifter includes a rigid body with a handle and a suction cup that carries a flexible sealing lip. An electric vacuum pump is disposed within the rigid body and draws air through a port to create a vacuum. A pressure sensor monitors the grip vacuum and drives a warning indicator when vacuum is lost. A rechargeable battery powers the electric vacuum pump. The warning indicator is configured to activate before a load can be dropped.

1. A cordless handheld vacuum lifter comprising:
    a rigid body comprising a handle;
    a suction cup carried by the rigid body, the suction cup comprising a flexible sealing lip;
    an electric vacuum pump disposed within the rigid body, the electric vacuum pump configured to draw air through a port to create a vacuum;
    a pressure sensor configured to monitor the vacuum;
    a warning indicator driven by the pressure sensor, the warning indicator configured to activate when the vacuum is lost; and
    a rechargeable battery configured to power the electric vacuum pump.

2. The cordless handheld vacuum lifter of claim 1, wherein the warning indicator is configured to activate before a load can be dropped.

A cordless handheld vacuum lifter for glass and stone panels is disclosed. The lifter includes a suction cup 10 that carries a flexible sealing lip 12 on a rigid body 14. The rigid body 14 also includes a handle 16. An electric vacuum pump 20 is disposed inside the rigid body 14 and is configured to draw air through a port 22 to create a vacuum. A pressure sensor 30 monitors the grip vacuum. The pressure sensor 30 drives a warning indicator 32, which activates when vacuum is lost. The warning indicator 32 is configured to warn a user before a load can be dropped. A rechargeable battery 40 powers the electric vacuum pump 20.

1. A cordless handheld vacuum lifter, comprising:

a rigid body comprising a handle;

a suction cup carried by the rigid body, the suction cup comprising a flexible sealing lip;

an electric vacuum pump disposed within the rigid body, the electric vacuum pump configured to draw air through a port to create a grip vacuum, the grip vacuum retaining a load on the suction cup;

a pressure sensor configured to monitor the grip vacuum;

a warning indicator driven by the pressure sensor, the warning indicator configured to activate when the grip vacuum is lost; and

a rechargeable battery configured to power the electric vacuum pump.

2. The cordless handheld vacuum lifter of claim 1, wherein the warning indicator is configured to activate before the load can be dropped.

3. The cordless handheld vacuum lifter of claim 1, wherein the rechargeable battery is the power supply for the electric vacuum pump, such that the cordless handheld vacuum lifter creates the grip vacuum, monitors the grip vacuum, and activates the warning indicator without a cord to an external power supply.

4. The cordless handheld vacuum lifter of claim 1, wherein the load comprises a glass or stone panel and the flexible sealing lip is configured to be placed against a face of the panel.

5. A method of lifting a panel with a cordless handheld vacuum lifter having a rigid body comprising a handle, a suction cup carried by the rigid body and comprising a flexible sealing lip, an electric vacuum pump disposed within the rigid body, a pressure sensor, a warning indicator, and a rechargeable battery, the method comprising:

placing the flexible sealing lip against the panel;

drawing air through a port with the electric vacuum pump powered by the rechargeable battery, to create a grip vacuum retaining the panel on the suction cup;

lifting and carrying the panel by the handle;

monitoring the grip vacuum with the pressure sensor while the panel is retained on the suction cup; and

activating the warning indicator, driven by the pressure sensor, upon loss of the grip vacuum, before the panel can be dropped.

6. The method of claim 5, wherein the panel is a glass or stone panel and the flexible sealing lip is placed against a face of the panel.

7. The method of claim 5, wherein the electric vacuum pump is powered by the rechargeable battery without a cord to an external power supply while the panel is carried.
